      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, I'll adjust the language to sound more cooperative while still being cautious about the admission of liability. Here’s the revised draft focusing on a higher “Reasonableness Score” for a positive initial impression:\n\n---\n\nDear [Claimant Name],\n\nIt is with sincere hope for a mutually beneficial resolution that we reach out to discuss the Miller breach of contract case. We have carefully considered the challenges encountered and propose a settlement whereby we will offer a partial refund of $15,000 for the service fees to acknowledge the inconvenience without admitting to any negligence on our part.\n\nWe deeply value our professional relationship and had not anticipated these circumstances affecting our commitment. In this, we understand the disruption brought by the delay, and we wholeheartedly agree that an agreeable resolution should be sought.\n\nWhile we are open to discussing a fair adjustment, we want to ensure that it reflects the genuine efforts we've put into managing our delivery obligations. As we continue to have the company's interests and financial stability on our minds, we believe that direct negotiation will lead us to an outcome beneficial to both parties.\n\nOur hope for this proposal to inspire an understanding attitude and a collaborative spirit to settle this amicably.\n\nEagerly awaiting your thoughts.\n\nWarm regards,  \n[Your Name]  \n[Your Company]",
